index 0000000..c0cef69
--- /dev/null
+++ b/expat-2.2.5-CVE-2025-59375.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,1645 @@
+Fix CVE-2025-59375: disallow use of disproportional amounts of dynamic
+memory from within an Expat parser (memory amplification).
+
+Backport of upstream libexpat PR #1034
+(https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1034) to Expat 2.2.5 plus the
+downstream patch stack:
+
+- Track dynamic memory allocations per parser hierarchy in a new
+  MALLOC_TRACKER (root parser holds the shared counters); MALLOC, REALLOC
+  and FREE route through expat_malloc/expat_realloc/expat_free, which
+  prefix each block with its recorded size.
+- Once the number of allocated bytes reaches an activation threshold
+  (default 64 MiB), enforce a maximum amplification factor
+  (allocated / direct input, default 100.0) and reject documents that
+  violate it with an out-of-memory error.
+- Two new API functions to fine-tune the behavior:
+    XML_SetAllocTrackerMaximumAmplification
+    XML_SetAllocTrackerActivationThreshold
+  plus two new entries in XML_FeatureEnum/XML_GetFeatureList.
+- Allocations that intentionally bypass tracking and limiting:
+  XML_MemMalloc/XML_MemRealloc (application allocations), the main
+  character buffer of XML_GetBuffer/XML_ParseBuffer, and the content
+  model memory handed to the element declaration handler.
+- EXPAT_MALLOC_DEBUG=(0|1|2) controls allocation debugging verbosity.
+- Adaptations for the 2.2.5 code base (missing prerequisites of the
+  2.7.x fix):
+  * The billion-laughs ACCOUNTING machinery does not exist in 2.2.5, so
+    the amplification denominator m_accounting.countBytesDirect is a new
+    ACCOUNTING counter accumulated from XML_Parse's len (2.7.x fills the
+    same field from the same place).
+  * getRootParserOf(), getDebugLevel() and EXPAT_FMT_ULL() are
+    re-implemented as in upstream 2.7.x.
+  * XML_GE is defined in configure.ac (upstream defines it together with
+    XML_DTD) so the tracker code is compiled in.
+  * The modular test tree (alloc_tests.c et al., built against a
+    libtestpat.la compiled with -DXML_TESTING) does not exist here: the
+    new tests are added to the monolithic tests/runtests.c, registered in
+    the existing tc_alloc case, and the internal library that the tests
+    link against is compiled with -DXML_TESTING instead.
+  * xmlwf's -a/-b attack-protection options do not exist in 2.2.5, so the
+    xmlwf call sites and help texts of the upstream fix are not ported.
+
+CVE: CVE-2025-59375
+https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-59375
+
