From 6f59f441228bc3d606b0c646c2f56d85e35fd1c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amalgamator Bench <amalgamator-bench@redhat.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:28:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] expat-cve-2025-59375-c8s: keep test-only helpers out of
 the shipped libexpat.so

The backport made libexpatinternal.la compile with -DXML_TESTING so that
tests/runtests.c can call expat_malloc/expat_free/expat_realloc directly.
Because libexpatinternal.la is also what the installed libexpat.la is
built from, that leaked the three test-only helpers into the exported
symbol table of the shipped libexpat.so (as verified with nm -D on the
built RPM payload).  Their names are generic and preemptible, so any
application defining its own expat_malloc would silently interpose and
disable the CVE-2025-59375 protection.

Match upstream's approach instead: build a separate, non-installed
libtestpat.la (compiled with -DXML_TESTING) and link the test programs
against that, while libexpatinternal.la -- and therefore the shipped
libexpat.so -- stays free of the testing symbols.

Verified: nm -D on the RPM payload's libexpat.so.1.6.7 now shows only
XML_SetAllocTrackerMaximumAmplification and
XML_SetAllocTrackerActivationThreshold as net-new exported symbols
(besides XML_SetReparseDeferralEnabled from the pre-existing
CVE-2023-52425 patch), and make check still passes 368/368 checks for
both runtests and runtestspp.
---
 expat-2.2.5-CVE-2025-59375.patch | 57 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/expat-2.2.5-CVE-2025-59375.patch b/expat-2.2.5-CVE-2025-59375.patch
index c0cef69..f751488 100644
--- a/expat-2.2.5-CVE-2025-59375.patch
+++ b/expat-2.2.5-CVE-2025-59375.patch
@@ -35,8 +35,11 @@ downstream patch stack:
   * The modular test tree (alloc_tests.c et al., built against a
     libtestpat.la compiled with -DXML_TESTING) does not exist here: the
     new tests are added to the monolithic tests/runtests.c, registered in
-    the existing tc_alloc case, and the internal library that the tests
-    link against is compiled with -DXML_TESTING instead.
+    the existing tc_alloc case, and -- as upstream does with its
+    libtestpat.la -- the tests link a separate, non-installed copy of the
+    library (libtestpat.la) compiled with -DXML_TESTING, so that the
+    test-only helpers expat_malloc/expat_free/expat_realloc stay out of
+    the shipped libexpat.so.
